> On Thursday, August 21, 2014 8:56:17 AM UTC-4, Pierre Abbat wrote:
>>
>> On Thursday, August 21, 2014 05:42:26 TR NS wrote:
>> > Does any one have *oral* conversations in Lojban?  More than a few
>> sentence?
>>
>> There are several Lojbanists in the Bay Area, and there's a Skype group.
>> I
>> think Arc Balandin is in charge of the Skype group. How much oral Lojban
>> actually happens, I don't know. I'm willing to talk Lojban on Skype, but
>> today
>> I'm going back home.
>>
>
> Actually, I was just wondering b/c I was reading about attitudinals and
> having a hard time imagining there is enough phonological "space" to be
> very clear when speaking, e.g. mishearing .u'o as u'u takes one from
> courage to repentance. That's a big difference in meaning for such a small
> phonological shift. I wonder about this with much of the language, but it
> stands out here in particular.
>

You can put the stress on {o} in {.u'o} but you must put a pause after
{.u'o} so it will all be {.u'O.} This makes recognition easier.

